   "question": "חשבו את הגבול הבא: $\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{4}{1+\\sqrt{9+x}}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{\\sin x}}$.",
   "solution": "$$L=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{4}{1+\\sqrt{9+x}}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{\\sin x}}=\\left[1^{\\infty}\\right]=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(1+\\frac{3-\\sqrt{9+x}}{1+\\sqrt{9+x}}\\right)^{\\frac{1+\\sqrt{9+x}}{3-\\sqrt{9+x}}\\cdot\\frac{3-\\sqrt{9+x}}{1+\\sqrt{9+x}}\\cdot\\frac{1}{\\sin x}}$$\n$$\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(1+\\frac{3-\\sqrt{9+x}}{1+\\sqrt{9+x}}\\right)^{\\frac{1+\\sqrt{9+x}}{3-\\sqrt{9+x}}}=e,$$\n$$\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{3-\\sqrt{9+x}}{1+\\sqrt{9+x}}\\right)\\frac{1}{\\sin x}=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{1}{\\left(1+\\sqrt{9+x}\\right)\\left(3+\\sqrt{9+x}\\right)}\\cdot\\frac{(-x)}{\\sin x}=\\frac{1}{4\\cdot6}\\cdot(-1)=-\\frac{1}{24}$$\n$$L=e^{\\left(-\\frac{1}{24}\\right)}$$",
