   "question": "חשבו את האינטגרל הבא: $\\int\\frac{dx}{x\\left(\\ln^2x-5\\ln x+6\\right)}$.",
   "solution": "$$\\int\\frac{dx}{x\\left(\\ln^2x-5\\ln x+6\\right)}=\\begin{vmatrix}t=\\ln x\\\\dt=\\frac{dx}{x}\\end{vmatrix}=\\int\\frac{dt}{t^2-5t+6}=\\int\\frac{dt}{(t-2)(t-3)}$$\n$$\\frac{1}{(t-2)(t-3)}=\\frac{A}{t-2}+\\frac{B}{t-3}=\\frac{A(t-3)+B(t-2)}{(t-2)(t-3)}\\ \\Rightarrow\\ A=-1,\\ B=1$$\n$$\\int\\frac{dt}{(t-2)(t-3)}=\\int\\left(-\\frac{1}{t-2}+\\frac{1}{t-3}\\right)dt=-\\ln|t-2|+\\ln|t-3|+C=\\ln\\left|\\frac{t-3}{t-2}\\right|+C$$\n$$\\int\\frac{dx}{x\\left(\\ln^2x-5\\ln x+6\\right)}=\\ln\\left|\\frac{\\ln x-3}{\\ln x-2}\\right|+C$$",
   "solutionSource": "official-pdf",
   "official": true,
