   "question": "חשבו את האינטגרל הבא: $\\int\\frac{dx}{\\sqrt[4]{x^3}\\left(\\sqrt{x}+2\\sqrt[4]{x}\\right)}$.",
   "solution": "$$\\int\\frac{dx}{\\sqrt[4]{x^3}\\left(\\sqrt{x}+2\\sqrt[4]{x}\\right)}=\\begin{vmatrix}x=t^4\\\\dx=4t^3dt\\end{vmatrix}=\\int\\frac{4t^3dt}{t^3\\left(t^2+2t\\right)}=4\\int\\frac{dt}{t(t+2)},$$\n$$\\frac{1}{t(t+2)}=\\frac{A}{t}+\\frac{B}{t+2}=\\frac{A(t+2)+Bt}{t(t+2)},\\quad A=\\frac12,\\ B=-\\frac12,$$\n$$\\int\\frac{dx}{\\sqrt[4]{x^3}\\left(\\sqrt{x}+2\\sqrt[4]{x}\\right)}=2\\int\\left(\\frac1t-\\frac{1}{t+2}\\right)dt=2\\left(\\ln|t|-\\ln|t+2|\\right)+C=2\\left(\\ln\\left|\\sqrt[4]{x}\\right|-\\ln\\left|\\sqrt[4]{x}+2\\right|\\right)+C=$$\n$$=\\frac12\\ln x-2\\ln\\left(\\sqrt[4]{x}+2\\right)+C$$",
   "solutionSource": "official-pdf",
   "official": true,
   "confidence": "high",
