   "question": "חשבו את האינטגרל $\\int\\frac{x^3+2x+5}{x^2-1}\\,dx$.",
   "solution": "חילוק פולינומים: $x^3+2x+5=x\\left(x^2-1\\right)+3x+5$, ולכן $\\frac{x^3+2x+5}{x^2-1}=x+\\frac{3x+5}{(x-1)(x+1)}$.\nפירוק לשברים חלקיים: $\\frac{3x+5}{(x-1)(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+1}$, כלומר $3x+5=A(x+1)+B(x-1)$.\n$x=1$: $8=2A\\Rightarrow A=4$. $x=-1$: $2=-2B\\Rightarrow B=-1$.\n$$\\int\\frac{x^3+2x+5}{x^2-1}\\,dx=\\int\\left(x+\\frac{4}{x-1}-\\frac{1}{x+1}\\right)dx=\\frac{x^2}{2}+4\\ln|x-1|-\\ln|x+1|+C$$",
   "solutionSource": "solved",
   "official": false,
   "confidence": "high",
   "part": "ב",
   "points": 10,
   "id": "20B-C-Q2b",
   "partKey": "b",
